#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_nonnegative

#% text
# `is_nonnegative(x)` gives `true` when `x` is a real at least 0, `false` when it is known not to be, and stays unevaluated when neither is decided.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Numbers and closed numeric expressions are decided by numerical bounds; symbols by the assumptions in force.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_nonnegative(0)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_nonnegative(-1)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_nonnegative(sqrt(2) - 1)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_nonnegative(x)
#% output
#= is_nonnegative(x)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Decided by assumptions:

#% cell
assuming(element(x, reals), is_nonnegative(x^2))
#% output
#= true

#% cell
assuming(x >= 0, is_nonnegative(x + 1))
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_positive`, `is_negative`, `assuming`
